{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY HITS ---\\\\n' && rg -n -i 'stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization|P56R|Aristotle closeout|two-lane|Lane H' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -80 && printf '\\\\n--- ROOT STATUS ---\\\\n' && pwd && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n\n--- MEMORY HITS ---\n385:# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n387:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n394:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n637:# Task Group: lean/stabilizer standalone Lean tensor-product and trace formalization\n640:applies_to: cwd=lean/stabilizer (source context=source-workspace); reuse_rule=reuse the checked algebraic modules and analytic-obligation checklist only after rechecking pinned mathlib and source assumptions\n646:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, partial: algebraic results checked; full theorem blocked)\n656:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, blocked: source and library lack required analytic inputs)\n\n--- ROOT STATUS ---\nlean/stabilizer\n M PLAN.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\n M work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/UltraweakNormality.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? aristotle_tasks/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P56-regional-product-state-identity-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-closeout.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
