{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- AGENTS.md ---'; sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PLAN.md ---'; sed -n '1,320p' PLAN.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TWO-LANE DECISION ---'; sed -n '1,300p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PACKET ---'; sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- STATUS/HANDOFF CANDIDATES ---'; find . -maxdepth 3 -type f \\\\( -iname '*status*' -o -iname '*handoff*' -o -iname 'PROGRESS*' -o -iname 'INTERACTION*' -o -iname 'README*' -o -iname 'SOURCE-CONTRACT*' -o -iname 'CONTEXT-LEDGER*' \\\\) -print | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- AGENTS.md ---\n# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n--- PLAN.md ---\n# Active plan: two-lane stabilizer-algebra formalization\n\n## Decision — 2026-08-07\n\nThe project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\nstabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\nsilently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n\n### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n\nFor a general consistent stabilizer system and region, construct the decreasing\nlocal-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\ntracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\nand derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n\nThis lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\nseparate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\nof a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\nmerely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n\n### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n\nFrom a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\ntheir coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\nmodels, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\nthe special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n\n`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n\nAfter proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\ntrivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\nnot follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\nspatial factorization.\n\n### Reconnection\n\nLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\nconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\nthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\nthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\nthe two results remain logically independent.\n\n## Aristotle package sequence\n\n### Shared/central core\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n\n### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Retired partial result: it proves the finite-word/algebraic state equality and conditional continuous-extension uniqueness, but does not prove C-star boundedness or positivity. |\n| P56R | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Recovery after P55D: construct the pure/mixed product C-star state from finite-dimensional density-matrix estimates, prove positivity/unitality and transport it through `alpha`; no supplied norm bound. |\n| P57A | `VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` | Shared infrastructure: port and audit the proved finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core from `bound_beating`; do not import external projects or package a completion as an axiom. |\n| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | After P54, P56R, and P57A, construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n\n### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n\n## Initial parallel wave\n\nSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\nand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   traciality and faithfulness.\n8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   integrated and audited.\n9. P56 is preserved as a partial artifact, not accepted evidence: its\n   `ProductStateBound` is an explicit missing C-star norm estimate and it has\n   no positivity theorem. P56R must derive the bound and positivity from the\n   finite-dimensional density-matrix data and P55D's concrete C-star model;\n   it may not use `ProductStateBound` in its final declarations or proofs.\n10. P57A may reuse the algorithmic finite-support construction in\n    `bound_beating/formalize_itp`, but only by an audited local port. It may\n    not import that separate project, copy its optional completion/axiom\n    wrappers, or claim a completed Hilbert tensor product before the quotient\n    and completion API is actually proved.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n\n1. Split coordinate indices into pure and mixed sectors.\n2. Establish the infinite-product GNS factorization.\n3. Identify the pure sector as `B(K_pure)`.\n4. Identify the mixed sector as a finite matrix factor when finite, or the\nhyperfinite `II_1` factor when infinite.\n5. Establish the spatial tensor-product identification of the product\nrepresentation.\n\n**Gate D:** every analytic theorem is either formalized against a supported\nMathlib API or recorded as an exact external theorem with source locator and\nexplicit hypothesis.\n\n## Phase E — theorem and trace corollaries\n\n1. Transport the Phase-D product classification through the Phase-C GNS\nunitary to the regional von Neumann algebra.\n2. State the finite-pure and infinite-pure cases separately.\n3. Finite pure sector: derive the normalized tracial-state conclusion.\n4. Infinite pure sector: state the faithful normal semifinite trace/weight\nconclusion; do not call it a tracial state.\n5. Audit every conclusion against `main.tex:1740-1752` and record any required\nmanuscript correction separately.\n\n## Parallelization\n\nUntil Phase B is blocked on a single coherent-coordinate construction, run in\nparallel:\n\n- finite phase/cocycle verification;\n- finite adapted-coordinate/stabilizer-state verification;\n- finite inclusion/coherence lemmas;\n- Mathlib/API feasibility audits for C-star inductive limits and GNS products;\n- product mixed-sector classification/source work.\n\nDo not parallelize mutually dependent attempts at the same global `alpha`.\nEach new Aristotle packet must use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` and state its\nsource basis plus every auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Exit criterion\n\nCall the manuscript theorem formally established only when Gates A--D are\ndischarged and Phase E compiles without substituting supplied interfaces for\nthe central finite-coordinate, C-star-extension, state-identity, or\nproduct-classification claims.\n--- TWO-LANE DECISION ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-10: P56 is retained as a partial, reviewed artifact. Its\nfinite-word and algebraic direct-limit identities are useful, but its concrete\nextensions depend on `ProductStateBound` and no positivity theorem was proved.\nP56R replaces it as the Lane-H state gate and must derive a genuine unital\npositive C-star functional directly from the finite pure/mixed density-matrix\ndata and the P55D concrete alpha. The original P56 job is disabled rather than\nrewritten, so the distinction remains machine-visible.\n\nIn parallel, P57A ports the *proved* finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite\ntensor pre-Hilbert construction from the compatible Lean-4.28 `bound_beating`\nworkspace into this repository as shared infrastructure. This is a local port,\nnot a cross-project import. Its optional completion/axiom wrapper is explicitly\nexcluded: P57A can establish the algebraic kernel, finite-mode realization,\npositivity, sesquilinearity, and pre-inner-product core, but the completed\nHilbert-space and spatial tensor claims remain P57 work and must be proved\nagainst the local Mathlib API.\n--- PACKET ---\n# P56R — recovered regional C-star product state\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1921-1946`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P56R`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P55D`, integrated and locally audited. `P56` is a\n  preserved partial artifact, not a predecessor or accepted result.\n- **Gate discharged:** construct the pure/mixed product **C-star state** and\n  prove that the regional state transported through the exact P55D C-star\n  alpha agrees with it.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no GNS tensor splitting, von Neumann\n  spatial tensor product, factorhood, center statement, or trace/weight\n  classification.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nEdit only `AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`. Keep its\nexisting finite-word and algebraic state-identity lemmas, but add a recovery\nsection whose final declarations have **no** `ProductStateBound` argument or\nother supplied boundedness/positivity premise.\n\nStarting from the checked one-qubit pure/mixed density matrices and the P55D\nconcrete source C-star model, prove the finite-stage product functional is\nunital and positive and has C-star norm at most one. Use the coherent direct\nlimit and the isometric dense source embedding to construct a continuous\nfunctional `cstarProductStateRecovered` on the concrete source C-star algebra.\nProve it is unital and positive (positivity on every `a† * a`, or the pinned\nMathlib positive cone if available), and transport it through\n`cstarAlpha.symm` to a unital positive\n`cstarRegionalStateRecovered`. Finally prove\n\n`cstarRegionalStateRecovered (cstarAlpha T) = cstarProductStateRecovered T`.\n\nIf the local project lacks a suitable state predicate, define a small local\npredicate whose content is precisely unitality plus positivity on squares;\nprove all of its fields. Do not package any of those fields as assumptions.\nDo not reuse `ProductStateBound` in a final recovery theorem, and do not merely\nrename its existence as an auxiliary structure.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nNone beyond P55D and the already checked finite pure/mixed one-qubit data.\nIf a required finite-dimensional C-star estimate cannot be derived from local\nMathlib and the existing finite-stage model, report the exact lemma/API gap and\nleave this recovery gate unaccepted; do not add an axiom, `sorry`, `admit`,\nopaque interface, or extra premise.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nEdit only `AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`. Retain its\nexisting imports and add only pinned local/Mathlib imports needed for a proved\nfinite-dimensional positivity or norm argument. Do not edit P55D, the\nmanuscript, another candidate, or an external project.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity` succeeds.\n- New recovery declarations do not depend on `ProductStateBound`.\n- The exact finite-stage norm/positivity lemma, source C-star extension,\n  unitality/positivity proofs, and alpha-transport identity are reported\n  separately.\n- No `sorry`, `admit`, new axiom, supplied state, or supplied completion is\n  introduced.\n- The response confirms the lane, predecessor, gate, and forbidden-claim\n  boundary.\n--- STATUS/HANDOFF CANDIDATES ---\n./CONTEXT-LEDGER.md\n./PROGRESS.md\n./README.md\n./SOURCE-CONTRACT.md\n./aristotle_tasks/README.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PROGRESS.md ---'; sed -n '1,320p' PROGRESS.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- README.md ---'; sed -n '1,240p' README.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CONTEXT-LEDGER.md ---'; sed -n '1,260p' CONTEXT-LEDGER.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SOURCE-CONTRACT.md ---'; sed -n '1,240p' SOURCE-CONTRACT.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- RECENT CLOSEOUTS ---'; for f in reviews/P55D-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md reviews/P56-regional-product-state-identity-closeout.md reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md; do echo \\\"### \"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,280p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PROGRESS.md ---'; sed -n '1,320p' PROGRESS.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- README.md ---'; sed -n '1,240p' README.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CONTEXT-LEDGER.md ---'; sed -n '1,260p' CONTEXT-LEDGER.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SOURCE-CONTRACT.md ---'; sed -n '1,240p' SOURCE-CONTRACT.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- RECENT CLOSEOUTS ---'; for f in reviews/P55D-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md reviews/P56-regional-product-state-identity-closeout.md reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md; do echo \\\"### \"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,280p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"--- PROGRESS.md ---\n# Formalization progress\n\n## Context policy (2026-08-05)\n\nAll future manuscript-facing formalization takes its context only from\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, with exact locators in the manuscript `main.tex`. Earlier\ngLU/refinement/layer-coherence artifacts remain available only as explicitly\nlabelled legacy infrastructure; they are not manuscript hypotheses. See\n`AGENTS.md` and `CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`.\n\nThe manuscript-facing module sequence is now `Formalization.Manuscript`:\nsource boundary, finite model, algebraic limit, product state, conditional GNS\nbridge, trace dichotomy, and only then the pending theorem contract. Existing\nimplementation files remain in place and are imported through facades.\n\n- P17 — under a supplied finite adapted-coordinate/word realization, the\n  finite pure/mixed product state is exactly the stabilizer indicator on every\n  supplied source Pauli basis word.\n- P18 — a supplied finite matrix-factor tensor decomposition transports the\n  finite product trace to an algebraic tracial state with its elementary-tensor\n  formula.\n- P19 — a supplied C-star model plus compatible states packages the existing\n  GNS unitary and algebraic commutant transport into one bridge interface.\n- P23 — supplied coherent finite-stage star equivalences induce the infinite\n  algebraic direct-limit regional equivalence `alpha`, with finite-stage and\n  inverse formulas. No C-star or von Neumann extension is claimed.\n- P24 — compatible target-stage algebraic states pull back along `alpha` to a\n  unique algebraic direct-limit state with its exact finite-stage expectation\n  formula and conditional stabilizer-indicator corollary.\n- P25 — supplied C-star completions and an extension of `alpha` yield an\n  isometric continuous C-star equivalence and continuous state pullback;\n  existence of those completions remains an explicit assumption.\n\n## Checked Lean results\n\n- `TPT-001` / `TPT-002` — an algebraic tracial state pulls back along a\n  complex `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- TPT-003 — algebraic traciality is reflected as well as preserved by a\n  complex star-algebra equivalence; hence a nontracial product state cannot\n  become tracial after an algebraic coordinate identification.\n- `FMT-001` — the normalized trace on a nonempty finite full matrix algebra is\n  an algebraic tracial state.  Positivity is proved by the explicit\n  trace-of-a-star-square sum-of-squares identity.\n- `FSC-001` — a finite corner equipped with a star isomorphism to a full matrix\n  algebra inherits that algebraic tracial state.\n- `FTT-001` — the finite algebraic tensor product of two matrix factors is\n  identified by the Kronecker star isomorphism, and its normalized trace\n  factorizes on elementary tensors; tensoring with a matrix identity preserves\n  the trace.\n- `FAM-001` — if `R` has an algebraic tracial state, then its finite matrix\n  amplification `Matrix n n R` has the normalized diagonal tracial state.\n  Positivity is checked as a finite sum of coefficient-algebra star-squares.\n  An explicit `StarAlgEquiv` transports this finite type-I product trace to a\n  target algebra.\n- `TMT-001` — the finite type-I product is now identified canonically, not\n  supplied as an assumption: `Matrix n n ℂ ⊗[ℂ] R` is star-isomorphic to\n  `Matrix n n R`.  Its trace factors on elementary tensors as the normalized\n  matrix trace times the coefficient trace.\n- `DTT-001` — the actual dyadic finite-stage system is constructed as\n  `A₀ = ℂ`, `Aₙ₊₁ = Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Aₙ`, with diagonal identity-qubit\n  embeddings.  Its normalized traces are compatible with every stage map,\n  and their algebraic directed limit carries the induced algebraic tracial\n  state.\n- FPU-001 — for every nonempty finite matrix factor, its algebraic tensor\n  product with the concrete dyadic algebraic limit carries the checked product\n  tracial state.  The theorem includes the elementary-tensor formula\n  tr_p(a) times qubitUHFTrace(u).\n- FPU-002 — any supplied regional `StarAlgEquiv` into that finite-pure\n  product model induces an algebraic tracial state on the regional algebra,\n  with the checked formula on inverse images of elementary tensors.\n- `AIT-001` — compatible unital cyclic finite-stage functionals glue to a\n  unital cyclic linear functional on mathlib's algebraic directed direct\n  limit.\n- `AIT-002` — compatible stagewise star-algebra maps induce an involutive,\n  additive, multiplication-reversing star on that algebraic direct limit.\n  Compatible algebraic tracial states then glue to an ordinary algebraic\n  tracial state there.\n- `SPC-001` — an adapted Hamel basis identifies the label space with finitely\n  supported X/Z coordinate labels and maps the singleton coordinate labels to\n  the chosen basis vectors.\n- ASC-001 — for a selected set of Z coordinates, Lean now identifies the\n  corresponding coordinate subspace both as the span of those Z basis\n  vectors and as the finite words with no X coordinate and no Z coordinate\n  outside the selected set.  This is the exact linear selection criterion\n  required before comparing the regional stabilizer state with the\n  pure/mixed product state.\n- FQS-001 — Lean now reads the recursive finite-qubit Pauli label as its\n  finite X/Z coordinate list and proves that the pure/mixed product-state\n  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n  separate obligation.\n\n## The exact theorem still to prove\n\nThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\nisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\nnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\nthe following essential premises open:\n\n1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   an exhaustion;\n2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   coordinate states; and\n5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n\nThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\nvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\nNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\nclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\ntarget theorem.\n\n## Last verification\n\n```text\nlake build\nlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.TraceTransport Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CoherentBasisEquiv Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.PureCoordinateNotTracial Formalization\nlake build Formalization.AdaptedStabilizerSubspace Formalization\nlake build Formalization.FiniteQubitPauliSelection Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CStarEquivExtension Formalization\nlake build AristotleCandidates.CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility AristotleCandidates.FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl\nlake env lean /tmp/stabilizer_hyperfinite_axioms_run4.lean\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error .../001-tensor-product-trace.tex\n```\n\nLean reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` for the\nchecked tensor-amplification, concrete dyadic direct-limit trace,\nfinite-support quadratic-phase, induced-trace, finite-qubit Pauli-word,\npure/mixed product-state, basis-level coherence, phase-corrected direct-limit\nequivalence/state transport, and properly-infinite trace-obstruction theorems.\nNo source theorem contains `sorry`, `admit`, or a user-declared axiom.  The\nblueprint build output is kept under `/tmp`, not in this source project.\n--- README.md ---\n# Stabilizer Hyperfinite Formalization\n\nThis is a standalone Lean project.  It is deliberately outside the Overleaf\ncheckout and does not edit the manuscript.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe source claim is the proposed normal `*-isomorphism`\n\n\\[\n  \\mathcal M_\\Gamma \\cong \\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)\\,\\bar\\otimes\\,\\mathcal R,\n\\]\n\nwhere `\\mathcal R` is the hyperfinite type `II_1` factor.  This project\nformalizes the algebraic transport lemma and a concrete dyadic finite-stage\ntrace system.  It does not identify a regional von Neumann algebra with a\ncompleted hyperfinite factor: that operator-algebraic identification remains\nan explicit interface until its missing compatibility assumptions are proved.\n\nThe project distinguishes two cases which the manuscript had conflated:\n\n* if `\\mathcal K` is finite dimensional, the tensor-product trace can be a\n  normal tracial state;\n* if `\\mathcal K` is infinite dimensional, `\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)` has no\n  tracial state.  The corresponding tensor-product trace is semifinite, not a\n  state.\n\n`Formalization/ProperlyInfiniteTraceObstruction.lean` checks the algebraic\ncore of this second point: two isometries with range projections summing to\nthe identity contradict a unital cyclic trace, hence also an algebraic\ntracial state.  Connecting that abstract criterion to a particular infinite\nvon Neumann representation remains analytic work.\n\nThe manuscript-only source contract is in `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. The source and\nproof-audit record is in `blueprints/001-tensor-product-trace.tex`. Earlier\ngLU/refinement artifacts are retained as legacy infrastructure only; see\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`.\n\n## Module map\n\n`Formalization.Manuscript` is the manuscript-facing Lean entry point. It orders\nthe project as `SourceDefinitions`, `FiniteModel`, `AlgebraicLimit`,\n`ProductState`, `GNSBridge`, `TraceDichotomy`, and `TheoremContract`.\n`Formalization.Infrastructure` exposes reusable checked material without a\nmanuscript claim. `Formalization.Legacy` is an opt-in aggregate for quarantined\nexploratory modules and is not imported by `Formalization.lean`.\n\n## Current checked result\n\n`Formalization/TraceTransport.lean` proves that an algebraically positive,\nunital tracial functional pulls back along a `StarAlgEquiv` to an algebraic\ntracial state, and that traciality is reflected by such an equivalence.  Thus\na nontracial product state cannot become tracial merely by changing\ncoordinates.  No axiom, `sorry`, or unproved model-factor classification is\nused by these theorems.\n\n`Formalization/FiniteMatrixTrace.lean` proves that the normalized trace on a\nnonempty finite full matrix algebra is an algebraic tracial state, including\npositivity through an explicit sum-of-squares calculation.\n\n`Formalization/FiniteCornerTrace.lean` transports that checked finite trace to\nany finite corner supplied with an explicit `StarAlgEquiv` to a full matrix\nalgebra.\n\n`Formalization/FiniteTensorTrace.lean` identifies the finite algebraic tensor\nproduct of two matrix factors through the Kronecker `StarAlgEquiv` and proves\nthe product-trace formula on elementary tensors.\n\n`Formalization/MatrixOverTrace.lean` proves the finite type-I amplification\nlemma in the needed noncommutative form: for an algebraic tracial state\n`tau : R -> ℂ`, the normalized diagonal functional on `Matrix n n R` is an\nalgebraic tracial state.  It then transports this trace along an explicitly\nsupplied `StarAlgEquiv` into the target regional algebra.\n\n`Formalization/TensorMatrixEquiv.lean` proves the canonical algebraic\nstar-isomorphism\n`Matrix n n ℂ ⊗[ℂ] R ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix n n R`, rather than assuming a finite\nproduct identification as data.  It proves the induced product-trace formula\non elementary tensors.\n\n`Formalization/DyadicTensorTower.lean` builds the concrete finite qubit tower\nin iterated matrix-amplification form, with the diagonal embeddings that\ncorrespond to adjoining an identity qubit.  It proves finite-stage trace\ncompatibility for all inclusions and constructs an algebraic tracial state on\nthe resulting directed algebraic limit.  This is the algebraic infinite qubit product,\nnot its C-star or von Neumann completion.\n\n`Formalization/SingleQubitPauli.lean` and\n`Formalization/FiniteQubitPauli.lean` make the finite target stages concrete:\nthey prove the ordered one-qubit Pauli multiplication and star phases, its\nfour-element complex basis, and their recursive finite-stage analogues.  The\ndyadic identity embeddings preserve these words and their phases.  This\neliminates the former finite-stage target-side Pauli-basis assumption.  A\nsingle global target word system and the matching regional source data remain\nseparate obligations.\n\n`Formalization/QubitMatrixState.lean` and\n`Formalization/FinitePureMixedQubitState.lean` formalize the state actually\nsuggested by an adapted stabilizer coordinate decomposition.  A Boolean\ncoordinate pattern selects either the `|0⟩` vector state or the normalized\nqubit trace at each finite stage.  These states are positive, compatible with\nthe dyadic embeddings, and therefore define an algebraic state on the UHF\ndirect limit.  The value on every finite Pauli word is explicit.  When every\ncoordinate is mixed, this is exactly `qubitUHFTrace`; when a pure coordinate is\npresent it is not promoted to a tracial state.  More precisely, a pure\ncoordinate permits only a zero X exponent, whereas a mixed coordinate permits\nonly the identity Pauli word.  Lean proves the expected obstruction already\nfor one pure qubit, and now for an arbitrary pure coordinate in the direct\nlimit: its vector-state factor is not cyclic, hence is not tracial.  Thus the\nalgebraic UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is\nmixed, precisely when it equals the checked UHF trace.\n\n`Formalization/AlgebraicLimitStateTransport.lean` transports this compatible\nstate family across any coherent finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv` family.  It is the\nformal conditional bridge from a regional finite-coordinate construction to\nthe corresponding quasi-local algebraic state.\n\n`Formalization/CoherentBasisEquiv.lean` and\n`Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean` make that coherence condition\nfinite and checkable.  If a finite-stage coordinate equivalence sends each\nsource basis word to a specified phase times a concrete finite Pauli word, and\nthe source-basis embedding, phase, and Pauli-label maps are coherent under\nenlarging the stage, Lean derives compatibility on every algebra element.\nThis gives a star-algebra equivalence of algebraic direct limits to the\nconcrete qubit-UHF algebra, then transports the pure/mixed product state and\nproves its exact value on each source basis word.  Its all-mixed\nspecialization pulls the UHF trace back to a source algebraic tracial state,\nand the corresponding pure/mixed source state is tracial exactly when all\ncoordinates are mixed.  This does not manufacture the required regional\ncoordinate bases or their coherence; it isolates those as the remaining\nfinite geometric inputs rather than assuming a global infinite map.\n\n`Formalization/FinitePureUHFProduct.lean` combines that concrete tracial\nalgebraic product with an arbitrary nonempty finite matrix factor.  It proves\nthe product algebraic tracial state and its elementary-tensor formula.  This\nis the formal finite-pure-sector analogue of the asserted tensor-product\ntrace, still before the UHF completion and normality statement.\n`Formalization/FinitePureUHFTraceTransport.lean` then proves the requested\ninduction step for any separately established regional `StarAlgEquiv`: it\npulls this product trace back to an algebraic tracial state on the region and\nretains the elementary-tensor formula on inverse images.\n\n`Formalization/SymplecticCoordinates.lean` proves the linear finite-word\nconsequence of an adapted Hamel basis: every label has a finitely supported\ncoordinate representative, and the chosen X/Z coordinate labels map to the\nspecified basis vectors.  `Formalization/AdaptedStabilizerSubspace.lean`\nthen proves the missing stabilizer-membership criterion: the selected\nZ-coordinate span contains exactly the finite words with no X coordinate and\nno Z coordinate outside the selected set.  `Formalization/PauliCocycleCompatibility.lean`\nthen proves the exact multiplier and involution phase equations required for\nsuch a coordinate map to respect Pauli-word multiplication and star.  These\nmodules deliberately do not call symplecticity alone a Pauli star-algebra\nisomorphism.  Formalization/StabilizerCharacterCalibration.lean proves\nthat the quotient of two multiplier phases is an ordinary additive character,\nthat an additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\nspace by a complementary-subspace construction, and that calibration by the\nextended Pauli-bit character preserves both the Pauli-word multiplication and\ninvolution compatibility equations.  This checks the algebraic\nstabilizer-sign calibration once the initial Pauli phase correction is\ngiven.  Formalization/FiniteSupportQuadraticRefinement.lean defines the\nblueprint's finite-support quadratic-refinement formula itself and proves its\nglobal polarization and diagonal identities.  Its explicit finite double-sum\ndiscrepancy pairing is additive in both arguments and symmetric for a\nsymmetric discrepancy.  Formalization/CoordinateQuadraticPhase.lean uses\nthese results to produce the required Pauli-word multiplication and star\ncompatibility certificates once the concrete source/target exponents are\nidentified with that pairing.  Together with\nFormalization/PhaseCorrectedWordBasisEquiv.lean, it gives a `StarAlgEquiv`\nbetween distinct source and target algebras whenever the phase-corrected word\nmap is supplied as a linear equivalence on a Pauli-word basis.  The remaining\nobligations are this concrete regional identification and the extension of\nwords to the quasi-local C-star algebra.\n\n`Formalization/FiniteQubitPauliSelection.lean` now identifies the recursive\nfinite-qubit label convention with this same selected-Z rule: a coordinate\nmarked pure has zero X exponent, while an unmarked (mixed) coordinate has the\nidentity label.  It proves that the finite pure/mixed Pauli expectation is the\nindicator of that condition, and identifies it with literal membership in the\nselected-Z submodule after an arbitrary supplied adapted coordinate basis.\n`CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean` consequently offers a source-basis expectation\nformula directly in terms of the selected-Z indicator, conditional on the\nalready explicit coherent finite-stage data.\nIt also has a theorem whose single additional premise is the actual regional\nmembership identification: selected target labels are exactly the source\nstabilizer basis words.  The conclusion is the phase-weighted stabilizer expectation\nformula on every basis word; completing this step requires an explicitly\nsupplied finite-coordinate construction, which the manuscript does not yet\nspecify.\n\n`Formalization/CoordinateQuadraticPhaseTrace.lean` composes this concrete\nphase result with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace construction: the same\nregional word-system, exponent, and basis hypotheses now produce both a\n`StarAlgEquiv` to `Matrix p p ℂ ⊗[ℂ] QubitUHFAlgebra` and the induced algebraic\ntracial state with its elementary-tensor formula.  The interface uses only a\n`Semiring` because that is the actual structure of the algebraic direct-limit\nmodel; no unproved additive-inverse structure is imposed.\n\nFormalization/WordBasisExtension.lean proves the algebraic extension step:\nwhen Pauli words form a complex linear basis, a linear map that preserves the\nproducts of all basis pairs is multiplicative on arbitrary finite sums and\ntherefore gives an algebra homomorphism if it is unital.  It also proves the\nconjugate-linear star extension: a bijective such map is a star-algebra\nequivalence when it commutes with star on basis words.\n\nFormalization/AlgebraicLimitStarHom.lean moves that finite-word result to\nthe algebraic quasi-local level.  It proves that compatible finite-stage\nstar-algebra maps induce a star-algebra map from the directed algebraic\nlimit, and that compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences induce a\nstar-algebra equivalence of the two algebraic limits.  Norm continuity and\ncompletion remain separate C-star obligations.\n\n`Formalization/CStarEquivExtension.lean` discharges the automatic part of\nthat analytic step: once the source and target have actually been supplied as\ncomplex C-star algebras, every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and hence\ncontinuous in both directions.  It also transports continuity of a target\nfunctional along the equivalence.  Constructing the required C-star norms and\ncompletions of the regional and coordinate direct limits remains open.\n\n`Formalization/AlgebraicInductiveTrace.lean` proves that any compatible system\nof finite-stage unital cyclic traces glues to a unital cyclic functional on its\nalgebraic direct limit.\n\n`Formalization/AlgebraicStarDirectLimit.lean` equips that algebraic direct\nlimit with the involution induced by compatible finite-stage star-algebra maps.\nIt proves that compatible algebraic tracial states glue to an ordinary\n`IsAlgebraicTracialState` on the limit.  This is the checked algebraic\ninfinite-product layer; no C-star or von Neumann completion is silently\nassumed.\n\n`Formalization/AlgebraicLimitTraceTransport.lean` adds the missing transport\nstep for a quasi-local algebraic factorization: compatible finite-stage\n`StarAlgEquiv`s and a compatible target tracial-state family induce a source\ndirect-limit tracial state, with its value on every finite-stage element fixed\nby the target-stage formula.  This is the exact algebraic statement required\nonce a stabilizer-region construction supplies coherent finite word maps.\n\n## Deliberate boundary\n\nMathlib 4.28 includes preliminary abstract and concrete von Neumann-algebra\ndefinitions, but its own basic module records the missing equivalence project.\n--- CONTEXT-LEDGER.md ---\n# Context ledger\n\n## Legacy exploratory material: not manuscript authority\n\nThe following artifacts contain gLU, refinement, or layer-coherence language\nimported from broader repository history rather than from the manuscript named\nin `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `blueprints/002-aristotle-parallel-formalization.tex`;\n- `aristotle_tasks/P6-layered-direct-limit.md`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/LayeredDirectLimit.lean`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/RegionalWitness.lean`; and\n- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean`.\n\nThey are preserved unchanged as useful exploratory or infrastructure work.\nThey may be cited only by a future task explicitly marked `Infrastructure\nonly`; they cannot establish a manuscript-derived hypothesis or conclusion.\n\n## Interpretation rule\n\nWhen an older document conflicts with `AGENTS.md` or `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, the\nnew manuscript-only policy governs all future task packets and reports. No\nhistorical label retroactively changes the source basis of a checked Lean\ntheorem.\n--- SOURCE-CONTRACT.md ---\n# Manuscript source contract\n\n## Authoritative source\n\n- Manuscript: `sources/manuscript/main.tex`\n- Title in source: *Infinite Magic and the Continuum* (`main.tex:117`)\n- Formalization policy: `AGENTS.md`\n\nThis project does not treat its own Lean files, prior agent prompts, or the\nsurrounding repository as mathematical source authority.\n\n## Source clauses in scope\n\n| Source locator | What the manuscript says | Formalization status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `main.tex:1671-1679` | Defines short-range order through a local symplectic basis, with `W_Gamma = span{z_i : i in P}` and finite support. | Requires a precise Lean model of the infinite Pauli/symplectic data. |\n| `main.tex:1740-1752` | States the short-range regional-algebra theorem, with an asserted factorization `A_Gamma` into a pure-sector type-I factor and a core factor that is finite type I or hyperfinite `II_1`. | Target statement; not established by current Lean artifacts. |\n| `main.tex:1915-1920` | Proposes an adapted symplectic basis and a star-isomorphism from an infinite Pauli algebra to `A_Gamma`. | External assumption/gap until the source construction is formalized. |\n| `main.tex:1927-1931` | Writes a pure/mixed product density state. | Finite density-matrix fragments are formalized; the infinite model is not. |\n| `main.tex:1945-1967` | Proposes the GNS/tensor-factor and type conclusions. | Conditional GNS transport is formalized; analytic product and type conclusions are not. |\n| `main.tex:1970-2004` | Proposes quasi-equivalence and normal-folium transport. | Not formalized. |\n\nThe wording above is a locator-oriented paraphrase, not a replacement for the\nmanuscript.\n\n## Permitted auxiliary assumptions\n\nAny manuscript-facing Lean theorem that needs one of the following must expose\nit in the theorem statement or task packet:\n\n1. a completed C-star or von Neumann algebra model for the infinite Pauli\n   system and its regional algebra;\n2. the asserted star-isomorphism from that model to the regional algebra;\n3. the product-state formula and hypotheses making the GNS representation a\n   spatial tensor product;\n4. the von Neumann closure, normality, and quasi-equivalence assumptions needed\n   to transport the claimed factor type; and\n5. any hyperfiniteness or trace theorem used for the core factor.\n\nNone of these assumptions is supplied merely by the phrase “short-range\norder” in the current manuscript source.\n\n## Trace correction\n\nThe manuscript-facing target must distinguish two cases:\n\n- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is finite-dimensional, a normalized tracial\n  state can be obtained from the finite matrix trace together with the core\n  trace;\n- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is infinite-dimensional, the appropriate\n  conclusion is a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight on the `II_infinity`\n  target, not a tracial state.\n\nThis is a correction to the intended theorem contract, not a claim that the\ncurrent manuscript already states or proves the corrected dichotomy.\n\n## Legacy firewall\n\nEarlier gLU/refinement/layer-coherence material is listed in\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`. It is retained, but it is neither a source clause nor an\nimplicit assumption of this formalization.\n--- RECENT CLOSEOUTS ---\n### reviews/P55D-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\nsed: can't read reviews/P55D-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md: No such file or directory\n### reviews/P56-regional-product-state-identity-closeout.md\n# P56 closeout review — regional/product-state identity\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: partial; queue must halt.**\n\nAristotle task `4b9085b9-015c-4c03-915b-46aa98784ff6` is terminal `COMPLETE`\nin `history/logs/20260808T204342Z-137c05f7-tasks.log`.\nIts exact archive alone was extracted into\n`aristotle_responses/P56-regional-product-state-identity-137c05f7-4b9085b9-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch ran in the dependency-free quarantine\nsnapshot. The sole packet-owned candidate module,\n`AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`, was copied into the\nlive project after review. The live and quarantined copies agree at SHA-256\n`39e430129834f067b1ee6942d2bf6acd74927c64b62ddc028949b6236cf7b176`.\nThe quarantined P55D and finite pure/mixed predecessor files are byte-identical\nto their live, accepted copies.\n\nThe candidate proves the requested finite-word and algebraic identities, but\ndoes **not** prove the required concrete C-star *state* identity. Its only\nconcrete construction requires the new premise\n`SourceConcreteRep.ProductStateBound`; moreover its constructed objects have\ntype `... →L[ℂ] ℂ`, with no positivity or C-star-state theorem. Therefore the\nreported C-star result is only a conditional equality of continuous linear\nfunctionals, not the state extension requested by P56. This is a meaningful\npartial artifact but does not discharge the P56 gate.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `A : AlphaData L I`, the candidate adds the following unconditional\nalgebraic results:\n\n- `allowedLabels`, `stabilizerLabels`, and\n  `coordinateMap_mem_stabilizerLabels_iff`;\n- `productExpectation`, `productExpectation_of_mem`, and\n  `productExpectation_of_not_mem`;\n- coherent unital linear functionals `sourceProductState` and\n  `regionalStabilizerState` on the algebraic direct limits;\n- `regionalStabilizerState_alpha_word` (finite Pauli words) and\n  `regionalStabilizerState_alpha` (the whole algebraic source limit);\n- stabilizer-word and unitality lemmas, including\n  `regionalStabilizerState_stabilizerElement`.\n\nThe density statement\n`SourceConcreteRep.cstarState_identity` is correct at its stated type: for\n*given* continuous linear maps `f` and `g` that agree with the two algebraic\nfunctionals on dense ranges, it proves `g (R.cstarAlpha T) = f T`. It also\nproves uniqueness of such maps.\n\nThe candidate then adds the new auxiliary structure\n`SourceConcreteRep.ProductStateBound`:\n\n```lean\nstructure ProductStateBound where\n  const : ℝ\n  norm_le : ∀ z : A.SourceLimit,\n    ‖A.sourceProductState z‖ ≤ const * ‖R.sourceEmbedding z‖\n```\n\nOnly under `hb : R.ProductStateBound` does it construct\n`cstarProductState hb`, `cstarRegionalState hb`, and prove\n`cstarRegionalState_cstarAlpha hb`. These are continuous linear functionals,\nnot formal C-star states: the module proves neither positivity nor the\nnorm-one/state property, and it does not derive `ProductStateBound` from the\nfinite density-matrix expectations and P55C representation.\n\nThe candidate inherits the already accepted P53/P55C/P55D conditional\ncoordinate and representation infrastructure. No axiom, sorry, admit, opaque,\nunsafe declaration, or forbidden downstream declaration was added.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite-word equality is proved in `regionalStabilizerState_alpha_word`; linear-basis extension proves the algebraic direct-limit identity `regionalStabilizerState_alpha`. The generic dense-range theorem `cstarState_identity` is also proved for already-continuous functionals. |\n| partial | The advertised concrete equality is conditional on the newly introduced `ProductStateBound`, which is not a locally integrated predecessor result. The constructed functionals have no proof of positivity, so Lean has not established either as a C-star state. |\n| blocked | P56's gate is not discharged: the missing boundedness/positive-state extension must be proved from the finite pure/mixed density-matrix states and the actual P55C C-star norm (or be made an explicitly approved new conditional downstream interface). P57 may not treat this module as an accepted state-identity predecessor. |\n| failed | No Lean build or placeholder failure occurred. The failure is semantic scope, not compilation. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met on finite Pauli words and on the\nalgebraic quasi-local limit. It is **not** met at the required concrete\nC-star-state scope.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P56, Lane H. This is correct.\n- **Predecessors:** the prepared packet incorrectly names retired `P55`.\n  The active `PLAN.md` and decision record require P55D. The candidate itself\n  imports `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha`, and P55D is locally integrated,\n  compiled, and semantically audited in\n  `reviews/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-closeout.md`; its archive copy\n  matches the accepted live file. The stale packet declaration is recorded and\n  has not been used as evidence.\n- **Permitted gate:** only the product-state equality after the exact P55D\n  alpha is in scope. The algebraic part is discharged; the concrete C-star\n  state-extension part remains conditional and therefore the gate is not\n  discharged.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module makes no GNS tensor\n  splitting, represented von Neumann/spatial tensor-product, factorhood,\n  trivial-center, trace, or weight conclusion.\n\n## Source alignment\n\nThe packet's source basis `main.tex:1915-1969` is accurate. In particular,\nthe finite-word selection/expectation argument is represented by\n`regionalStabilizerState_alpha_word`, matching `main.tex:1927-1943`. The\nmanuscript's passage from equality on Pauli-word bases to equality of the\nstates is represented only algebraically. Its C-star continuity/state\ncontent remains an auxiliary analytic obligation, not a manuscript-derived\nfact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity` — passed\n  (`8062/8062` jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity Formalization`\n  — passed (`8096` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed (up to date, `0` jobs).\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing the candidate and printing axioms for\n  `regionalStabilizerState_alpha_word`, `regionalStabilizerState_alpha`,\n  `cstarState_identity`, `cstarRegionalState_cstarAlpha`, and\n  `regionalCStarAlpha_state_identity` — each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate plus direct P55D and pure/mixed imports —\n  no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live hashes for the candidate and direct predecessors, and\n  `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nOne acceptance-blocking finding: lines 694--700 introduce rather than prove\nthe norm bound required to pass from the algebraic functional to a continuous\nC-star functional; lines 714--765 use that premise. Lines 647--657 prove a\nvalid uniqueness implication, but it assumes the continuous functionals\nalready exist. The module contains no positivity theorem (the objects are\ndeclared as continuous linear maps), so calling the final conditional result a\nstate identity would overstate the evidence.\n\nNo other scope, source-locator, forbidden-claim, axiom, or compilation defect\nwas found. The P53/P55D assumptions remain external conditional\ninfrastructure, as already recorded by their accepted closeouts.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the exact archive, its 223-file quarantine extraction,\nthe reviewed partial candidate, and this closeout. All modified plan/task/\ndecision files and pre-existing candidates/reviews remain untouched. No\nmanuscript file was modified; no commit, push, archive build, dependency\nupdate, or dependency fetch occurred.\n### reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md\n# P57A closeout review — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nAristotle task `563e769a-0e9b-4395-9895-e03c81c26851` was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a.tar.gz`\nand extracted, without a build, dependency update, or fetch, only under\n`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project.  The raw archive and quarantine extraction\nremain intact response records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n\nThe quarantined response incorrectly said that the nominated local source\n`<original-home>/Projects/current/bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean`\nwas absent.  It is present.  Local comparison confirms that the integrated\nmodule independently re-expresses the source's proved finite-support core,\nbut with a finite-Gram-coordinate proof route rather than importing the other\nproject.  I corrected that provenance comment in the live integrated module;\nthis changes documentation only.  The candidate and quarantine SHA-256 values\ntherefore differ:\n\n- live: `c4936227e370cd0d04c32f4d62807003ed688afba9ca661a330c696a5c75feca`;\n- quarantined response: `ee8862347e606cc8ac629e3baa8909354ad288da9a4f5502c8639fa595633c52`.\n\n## Source, assumptions, and exact declarations\n\nThis is **infrastructure only**, not a manuscript-facing assertion.  The\ncandidate imports only `Mathlib`; it does not import the `bound_beating`\nproject or any other package result.\n\nAll generic results use only the packet-authorized assumptions\n`[DecidableEq ι]`, `[∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)]`, and\n`[∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)]`.  The normalization premise\n\n```lean\nhΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1\n```\n\nis used exactly where padding a product outside active support, positivity,\nfinite-mode kernel realization, finite-mode evaluation, and the exported\npre-inner-product core require it.  No completion, density, positivity, or\nexternal analytical premise was added.\n\nThe load-bearing live declarations are:\n\n- `exists_gram_coords` (lines 64--77), finite coordinates for every finite\n  Gram matrix;\n- `exists_finiteMode_realization` (88--104) and\n  `sum_prod_inner_nonneg` (109--122), realizing the product kernel as a\n  norm square in a finite coordinate tensor model;\n- `VacuumTensor` (128--134), `kern` (153--154), and\n  `kern_eq_prod_of_subset` (158--164), defining the finite-support\n  elementary tensors and support-independent kernel;\n- `itpInner` (183--184), `conj_itpInner_symm` (220--231),\n  `itpInner_add_left` (234--247), and `itpInner_smul_left` (250--262),\n  the algebraic sesquilinear extension;\n- `itpInner_nonneg` (266--285), positivity for an arbitrary finite linear\n  combination, and `re_itpInner_nonneg` (288--291);\n- `itpCore` (295--301), the exported\n  `PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPSpan Ω)`;\n- `vacuumVector` and `itpInner_vacuumVector` (309--322), whose\n  norm-square is one; and\n- `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern` (329--341) and\n  `itpInner_eq_finiteMode` (344--352), the finite-mode statements for the\n  actual vacuum-restricted kernel and algebraic span.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite-support elementary tensors, their finite-product kernel, the free finite span, sesquilinearity, finite-mode realization, positivity on arbitrary finite sums, the pre-inner-product core, and the algebraic vacuum norm-square-one theorem are all explicit proved declarations. |\n| partial | Quotienting the null space, completion, and an infinite tensor-product Hilbert-space instance are deliberately absent. |\n| blocked | None at P57A scope.  The local Mathlib snapshot lacks a ready-made inner-product API for a general `PiTensorProduct`; the candidate avoids that gap by proving the finite Gram-coordinate realization in `EuclideanSpace`, which suffices for the stated kernel positivity theorem. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at the stated scope.  The changed\nroute is the finite-Gram-coordinate proof of positivity, instead of importing\nor copying an optional completion wrapper from the source workspace.  It adds\nno premises and neither weakens the algebraic target nor supplies a\ncompletion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P57A, Lane `shared` — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** none — correct.  The module is self-contained and imports\n  only Mathlib; it uses no package result that was merely remotely finished.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: it supplies a proved finite-support\n  vacuum-restricted algebraic ITP kernel and pre-inner-product core, so P57\n  need not recreate that algebraic layer.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module has no quotient or\n  completion, no completed infinite tensor-product Hilbert space, no\n  pure/mixed GNS tensor splitting, no spatial von Neumann tensor product, no\n  factor classification, and no manuscript state identity.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct` —\n  passed in the already-built live project (8026 jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `#print axioms` for `exists_gram_coords`,\n  `exists_finiteMode_realization`, `sum_prod_inner_nonneg`,\n  `kern_eq_prod_of_subset`, `itpInner_nonneg`, `itpCore`,\n  `itpInner_vacuumVector`, and `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern` —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- A forbidden-declaration scan found no `sorry`, `admit`, user\n  `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide`; the only textual matches are explanatory prose.\n- Direct-import audit: exactly `import Mathlib`; no external-project import.\n  `git diff --check` for the integrated module passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the normalization\npremise is used to justify only padding outside the finite active set, that\npositivity reduces the complete finite Finsupp support to an actual finite\ncoordinate norm square, and that the `PreInnerProductSpace.Core` receives\nthe real-part nonnegativity required by its interface.  It also checked the\nempty-active-set vacuum calculation separately, so its norm-square-one\nstatement is not being promoted to a general product-padding theorem without\n`hΩ`.  Builds and axiom reports validate the formal declarations, but do\nnot create the intentionally omitted quotient, completion, GNS, or spatial\noperator-algebra results.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P57A candidate, this closeout review, the\nexact raw archive, and its quarantine extraction.  The repository already had\nthe listed modified plan/task files and untracked earlier candidates/reviews;\nthey were not overwritten or otherwise changed.  No commit, push, archive\nbuild, dependency update, dependency fetch, or manuscript modification was\nperformed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
